{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.731177Z","id":"d98ab4255e278e6fbb4b1da311ff2e95afa031ccc93e29b5fc93b81214058577","body":{"detail":"A tab hidden for HIDDEN_MS (30 s) releases its topics and fetches its state again when it shows; the shared connection has no per-tab resume point.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":319},"end":{"line":338},"content_hash":"50c522e84cb5cdc1713ecbc3f861987420515d73d6fa24c51e8100ef15d8744e"},"suggested_fix":"Per-topic rings in the worker would let a briefly hidden tab replay instead.","summary":"A hidden tab's catch-up is a refetch","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:32:59.731211Z","id":"55c90b79a7e526231bc7e5ebdf5e0ac62f9a4eec00f9122f4bbf705541e6f834","body":{"detail":"A tab counts its hub gone after DEAD_MS (35 s) without a ping, or at once where the browser fires close on the worker's port. A worker that lives but hangs is not restarted, since a new SharedWorker of the same name reaches the same instance. Leader tabs are not pinged at all: a hidden leader's timers are throttled and its followers would replace it needlessly; a leader hidden for 30 s leaves, so a frozen tab does not hold the connection for long.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":440},"end":{"line":443},"content_hash":"3643dd1ee71089c5de9eefb664e36a0c9b7381f7a039d5bd1209b1a37d43fcdf"},"summary":"The shared worker is checked only by its pings; a hung worker is not restarted","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream-hub.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:26:52.183528Z","id":"af99e0847d6ce2acbeb8dc02c4fb0ecccc1422f8ce16b5f5205a33dc2489b39e","body":{"detail":"drop() aborts the current connection. When that connection is a GET /api/stream whose response has not reached the page yet, Chrome keeps the socket to drain the response for reuse (about 5 s; the SSE body never ends) and only then closes it, so the daemon counts the stream attached meanwhile (`open` and `levels` in GET /api/_test/stream/open). web/e2e/streams.spec.ts saw two admin streams for about 5 s this way when one rename caused several reopens. The hub now reopens once per caller change, so this remains only when a reopen lands while a connect is in flight. The daemon detaches a closed client within a millisecond; the delay is the browser's.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":461},"end":{"line":467},"content_hash":"50f43433859ae4b4960306f84d9917ae901ccd99c2692329e7e275099aa83ca7"},"summary":"A stream request aborted before it answers stays open on the daemon for up to 5 s","tags":["risk","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/owner.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:26:52.183696Z","id":"39039ebd109e36a9ab6fa0a5b16c7fbc7afba8fa60ff45ae6e1bb7110fbd04b0","body":{"detail":"After getToken() fails, ownerBrowser() retries with its own fetch of /api/token. When that succeeds the browser holds the events cookie, but api.ts's tokenPromise stays unset and its onToken listeners do not run, so the next getToken() fetches the token again, and the page's stream is reopened as the owner's only when the hub's next subscription on the old stream is refused (stream-hub.ts, unknown_stream) or a later getToken() succeeds. web/e2e/streams.spec.ts (the late-token test) shows the stream still reopening once.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":16},"end":{"line":19},"content_hash":"59b34f86a2eaf058ac291d8fa806118099047e4ca5716284f58f1e542cfb2ea4"},"suggested_fix":"Retry through getToken() (after its memo is dropped) so a success sets the memo and runs the onToken listeners.","summary":"ownerBrowser's own token retry leaves getToken's memo failed","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream-hub.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:35:49.946752Z","id":"8525f268fb8a05164766a18851d809e67ab80bd9ab2ce4b3200b0d7281681647","body":{"detail":"drop() aborts the current connection. When that connection is a GET /api/stream whose response has not reached the page yet, Chrome keeps the socket to drain the response for reuse (about 5 s; the SSE body never ends) and only then closes it, so the daemon counts the stream as attached meanwhile (`open` and `levels` in GET /api/_test/stream/open), holding a second stream for the browser. The hub reopens at most once per caller change (the `reconnect` case compares the asked caller with the one the stream's `ready` named), so this happens when a reopen, a reconnect after a refused subscription, or a failure's retry lands while a connect is in flight. The daemon detaches a closed client within a millisecond; the delay is the browser's.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":461},"end":{"line":467},"content_hash":"50f43433859ae4b4960306f84d9917ae901ccd99c2692329e7e275099aa83ca7"},"suggested_fix":"Let an in-flight connect reach its `ready` before acting on a reconnect or a refused subscription (decide then, as an ask made while no stream is up already is), so the hub never aborts a stream request that has not answered.","summary":"A stream request aborted before it answers stays open on the daemon for up to 5 s","supersedes":"af99e0847d6ce2acbeb8dc02c4fb0ecccc1422f8ce16b5f5205a33dc2489b39e","tags":["risk","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:38:28.460351Z","id":"0239b9e01e340c099e2641be35f6583631bb99281339a8f3de905ef92a9407ef","body":{"detail":"A tab hidden for HIDDEN_MS (30 s) releases its topics and fetches its state again when it shows; the shared connection has no per-tab resume point.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":323},"end":{"line":342},"content_hash":"50c522e84cb5cdc1713ecbc3f861987420515d73d6fa24c51e8100ef15d8744e"},"suggested_fix":"Per-topic rings in the worker would let a briefly hidden tab replay instead.","summary":"A hidden tab's catch-up is a refetch","supersedes":"d98ab4255e278e6fbb4b1da311ff2e95afa031ccc93e29b5fc93b81214058577","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-10T01:38:28.460429Z","id":"87de9a6414227d430f6a7a7d5c5361145e613d37bac16d2064315c645579a079","body":{"detail":"A tab counts its hub gone after DEAD_MS (35 s) without a ping, or at once where the browser fires close on the worker's port. A worker that lives but hangs is not restarted, since a new SharedWorker of the same name reaches the same instance. Leader tabs are not pinged at all: a hidden leader's timers are throttled and its followers would replace it needlessly; a leader hidden for 30 s leaves, so a frozen tab does not hold the connection for long.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":444},"end":{"line":447},"content_hash":"3643dd1ee71089c5de9eefb664e36a0c9b7381f7a039d5bd1209b1a37d43fcdf"},"summary":"The shared worker is checked only by its pings; a hung worker is not restarted","supersedes":"55c90b79a7e526231bc7e5ebdf5e0ac62f9a4eec00f9122f4bbf705541e6f834","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/waiting.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-11T02:46:09.795109Z","id":"b68a78ba03e7b2b67859cab95300df5a891e882c2852b57fb3b2752d4a23fce3","body":{"detail":"The daemon now reports state withheld with an approver name (crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs state_of) for a comment held from its agent until the agent's person approves its author; waitingLabel has no case for it, so the thread shows no waiting indicator. Spec §10 wants 'waiting for Sam's approval'. clax comments prints it (crates/clax-cli/src/commands/comments.rs delivery).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":34},"end":{"line":34},"content_hash":"94752ffd9323a0e85d941ed8b7de2099267ddbfee318f8338c4977428961c9be"},"summary":"The shell shows no delivery label for feedback_state withheld","tags":["people","ui","spec:10","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream-hub.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:04:39.286782Z","id":"a389fe86a5794375e200f440b6b0cc3f2f7d01702febcd91a16de7706d6b119a","body":{"detail":"drop() aborts the current connection. When that connection is a GET /api/stream whose response has not reached the page yet, Chrome keeps the socket to drain the response for reuse (about 5 s; the SSE body never ends) and only then closes it, so the daemon counts the stream as attached meanwhile (`open` and `levels` in GET /api/_test/stream/open), holding a second stream for the browser. The hub reopens at most once per caller change (the `reconnect` case compares the asked caller with the one the stream's `ready` named), so this happens when a reopen, a reconnect after a refused subscription, or a failure's retry lands while a connect is in flight. The daemon detaches a closed client within a millisecond; the delay is the browser's.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":477},"end":{"line":483},"content_hash":"50f43433859ae4b4960306f84d9917ae901ccd99c2692329e7e275099aa83ca7"},"suggested_fix":"Let an in-flight connect reach its `ready` before acting on a reconnect or a refused subscription (decide then, as an ask made while no stream is up already is), so the hub never aborts a stream request that has not answered.","summary":"A stream request aborted before it answers stays open on the daemon for up to 5 s","supersedes":"8525f268fb8a05164766a18851d809e67ab80bd9ab2ce4b3200b0d7281681647","tags":["risk","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:04:39.288387Z","id":"d8cce851555f951af6ccf1ae3b9dfe38ebb76efe1340bada4e9bc10a16ca795e","body":{"detail":"A tab hidden for HIDDEN_MS (30 s) releases its topics and fetches its state again when it shows; the shared connection has no per-tab resume point.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":330},"end":{"line":349},"content_hash":"50c522e84cb5cdc1713ecbc3f861987420515d73d6fa24c51e8100ef15d8744e"},"suggested_fix":"Per-topic rings in the worker would let a briefly hidden tab replay instead.","summary":"A hidden tab's catch-up is a refetch","supersedes":"0239b9e01e340c099e2641be35f6583631bb99281339a8f3de905ef92a9407ef","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:04:39.290026Z","id":"932a69a375afa3ab35f876ff67c6201fde3ec7fd4e715604f4bc917459b6d3df","body":{"detail":"A tab counts its hub gone after DEAD_MS (35 s) without a ping, or at once where the browser fires close on the worker's port. A worker that lives but hangs is not restarted, since a new SharedWorker of the same name reaches the same instance. Leader tabs are not pinged at all: a hidden leader's timers are throttled and its followers would replace it needlessly; a leader hidden for 30 s leaves, so a frozen tab does not hold the connection for long.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":451},"end":{"line":454},"content_hash":"3643dd1ee71089c5de9eefb664e36a0c9b7381f7a039d5bd1209b1a37d43fcdf"},"summary":"The shared worker is checked only by its pings; a hung worker is not restarted","supersedes":"87de9a6414227d430f6a7a7d5c5361145e613d37bac16d2064315c645579a079","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/owner.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:19:06.766550Z","id":"71fb8686842d19e8c5d54164b3fe1a79e76c68a7bcf5a8bb8a9eed70b683ad7b","body":{"detail":"ownerBrowser() and getToken() ask GET /api/token, which a hosted daemon answers 404 (crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs gate). The owner's session is Caller::Owner { browser: true } server-side, but routes taking RequireToken and the shell's token-gated controls stay unavailable. PeopleLink asks /api/hosted/me instead; nothing else does. The gallery header also still reads 'local artifacts'.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":12},"end":{"line":12},"content_hash":"ee86ee0c2175c338a5f64f0cf9a302155d98f2bfbc115f4118d64df71edf3701"},"suggested_fix":"Let the shell learn ownership from GET /api/hosted/me in hosted mode and send owner writes without the token where the daemon accepts the owner's browser.","summary":"A hosted owner's browser is never served the token, so the shell's owner surfaces that ask for it are off: the inbox and questions, rename, pin and delete","tags":["hosted","ui","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/owner.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:55:24.316274Z","id":"cb854195b3ab7ce6015b271925722d2d4f55f89ceafa52c941449b23bb6aa70a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:d44e6509","summary":"Fixed: GET /api/token hands a hosted owner's session its shell token (cxo_, an HMAC of the session cookie under a key made from the daemon token; crates/clax-server/src/hosted.rs shell_token, token_for), and the gate takes it beside that cookie (and the public Origin for a change) as the daemon token, in Authorization or a WebSocket's token parameter; anyone else gets 403 not_owner, so ownerBrowser() resolves. The gallery bar names the site. Evidence: api_hosted::the_owners_browser_holds_a_shell_token_that_stands_for_the_daemon_token passes (questions, inbox, people, rename, pin, delete; refused without the cookie, beside another browser's, without Origin, after sign out); web/e2e/hosted.spec.ts shows the bar 'localhost:<port> · seen as Ada', Pin and Inbox, and pins a page.","supersedes":"71fb8686842d19e8c5d54164b3fe1a79e76c68a7bcf5a8bb8a9eed70b683ad7b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/owner.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:34:48.162628Z","id":"50fbae8dc711f064037bc747aba83a54ee2a563dda7da6130d8f8ef2aed8dcad","body":{"detail":"After getToken() fails, ownerBrowser() retries with its own fetch of /api/token. When that succeeds the browser holds the events cookie, but api.ts's tokenPromise stays unset and its onToken listeners do not run, so the next getToken() fetches the token again, and the page's stream is reopened as the owner's only when the hub's next subscription on the old stream is refused (stream-hub.ts, unknown_stream) or a later getToken() succeeds. web/e2e/streams.spec.ts (the late-token test) shows the stream still reopening once.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":17},"end":{"line":20},"content_hash":"59b34f86a2eaf058ac291d8fa806118099047e4ca5716284f58f1e542cfb2ea4"},"suggested_fix":"Retry through getToken() (after its memo is dropped) so a success sets the memo and runs the onToken listeners.","summary":"ownerBrowser's own token retry leaves getToken's memo failed","supersedes":"39039ebd109e36a9ab6fa0a5b16c7fbc7afba8fa60ff45ae6e1bb7110fbd04b0","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream-hub.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:17:08.819479Z","id":"5870069c462f45753a3e950360e0868360aa8c04031b5c74a3593ea7d2478bcb","body":{"detail":"The hub learns that the server carries /api/stream over a WebSocket only from a 426 to the plain request, and remembers it for its own life: once per shared worker, but once per page load where the hub runs in the tab (no SharedWorker). The daemon is unaffected. A server that advertised the transport (in the /a/ bootstrap, or a header on a response the shell already makes) would save the round trip on the time-to-usable path.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":324},"end":{"line":328},"content_hash":"e461307789815f4359eb9af3636cda0d5096499a69ff787f40b9ab7f66444374"},"summary":"On a Worker each new stream hub pays one 426 round trip before it opens the WebSocket","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream-hub.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T06:18:39.905351Z","id":"e604b4be66fabd7e5bc699b25d1e319d606f305badbf0c33b7c9a9d04c740b3c","body":{"detail":"drop() aborts the current connection. When that connection is a GET /api/stream whose response has not reached the page yet, Chrome keeps the socket to drain the response for reuse (about 5 s; the SSE body never ends) and only then closes it, so the daemon counts the stream as attached meanwhile (`open` and `levels` in GET /api/_test/stream/open), holding a second stream for the browser. The hub reopens at most once per caller change (the `reconnect` case compares the asked caller with the one the stream's `ready` named), so this happens when a reopen, a reconnect after a refused subscription, or a failure's retry lands while a connect is in flight. The daemon detaches a closed client within a millisecond; the delay is the browser's.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":529},"end":{"line":535},"content_hash":"50f43433859ae4b4960306f84d9917ae901ccd99c2692329e7e275099aa83ca7"},"suggested_fix":"Let an in-flight connect reach its `ready` before acting on a reconnect or a refused subscription (decide then, as an ask made while no stream is up already is), so the hub never aborts a stream request that has not answered.","summary":"A stream request aborted before it answers stays open on the daemon for up to 5 s","supersedes":"a389fe86a5794375e200f440b6b0cc3f2f7d01702febcd91a16de7706d6b119a","tags":["risk","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/owner.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:46:43.168948Z","id":"5f5bc57859f2b885409663b911f557d29461631d62739169562fb16a9db8952d","body":{"detail":"After getToken() fails, ownerBrowser() retries with its own fetch of /api/token. When that succeeds the browser holds the events cookie, but api.ts's tokenPromise stays unset and its onToken listeners do not run, so the next getToken() fetches the token again, and the page's stream is reopened as the owner's only when the hub's next subscription on the old stream is refused (stream-hub.ts, unknown_stream) or a later getToken() succeeds. web/e2e/streams.spec.ts (the late-token test) shows the stream still reopening once.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":12},"end":{"line":14},"content_hash":"3583aab0722c57192d9777c50e3b423a5cb5f506f0d69f5340e6a13a39ff815d"},"suggested_fix":"Retry through getToken() (after its memo is dropped) so a success sets the memo and runs the onToken listeners.","summary":"ownerBrowser's own token retry leaves getToken's memo failed","supersedes":"39039ebd109e36a9ab6fa0a5b16c7fbc7afba8fa60ff45ae6e1bb7110fbd04b0","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/owner.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T03:46:43.169976Z","id":"731e8dc09a348b80609c99df62d4b1f0864b765b3a0e6eaf5a62440e9a50a493","body":{"detail":"inboxBrowser asks GET /api/inbox?limit=1 after the token is refused, so every page a LAN viewer opens makes one refused request (web/e2e/questions.spec.ts counts it). The gallery already fetches /api/viewers/me, whose viewer carries `person` for a connected person, so it could decide without the extra request; the inbox route answering is the authority on who has an inbox (a revoked person, a narrowed grant), which is why it is asked.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":22},"end":{"line":24},"content_hash":"1c00202836a1793c48a45e75bb5b9ea9a31c6d3a053fadc6a0cad12baf13b1b5"},"summary":"Know a connected person's browser from GET /api/viewers/me (its person flag) instead of a look at /api/inbox","tags":["revisit:LAN viewers' page loads become latency-sensitive, or /api/viewers/me gains an inbox flag","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/owner.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T04:48:04.741737Z","id":"27fc3c286225e165c7502d1475ea97fdb0a2db3ccd328f36759f36c872590399","body":{"detail":"On a scratch daemon a LAN viewer made exactly one refused GET /api/inbox?limit=1 per page (/inbox, /, /a/<id>), each logging a 'Failed to load resource: 403' console error beside the existing /api/token ones; nothing of the inbox rendered or leaked. For a connected person the look is a sequential round trip after the /api/token 403 and before the q chunk loads. web/shell/src/ui/Gallery.svelte:97 already fetches GET /api/viewers/me on every page, and its `person`/`person_revoked_at` fields (web/shell/src/people/PeopleLink.svelte:5) answer the same question with no extra request; the artifact view also knows its viewer before artifact-questions.ts runs. Recommendation: gate on the viewer's person flag, keeping /api/inbox's 403 as the authority when the feeds start.","kind":"comment","references":"731e8dc09a348b80609c99df62d4b1f0864b765b3a0e6eaf5a62440e9a50a493","summary":"Measured cost of the /api/inbox look, and why /api/viewers/me looks better","tags":["review","task:21","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/owner.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T05:16:17.637527Z","id":"a9690820535f9d2d5c60dff24ad9b6e66d928e36ee3ef014608a3fa47676d2cf","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a5019f38","span":{"start":{"line":22},"end":{"line":24},"content_hash":"9c970c33d9b46f3a88558e76a513e06786ad91e220ff45bdb65f608847714d05"},"summary":"Taken: inboxBrowser now reads the person flag of the page's own GET /api/viewers/me (the gallery's lookup, the artifact view's seeded viewer), else the owner's token; the inbox routes stay the authority when the feeds start. Evidence: e2e/questions.spec.ts, reverted to expect no /api/inbox or /api/questions request from a LAN viewer, passes; in Chromium a plain LAN viewer on /, /inbox and /a/<id> made none, and Ivy's and Jo's browsers made no /api/inbox?limit=1 look.","supersedes":"731e8dc09a348b80609c99df62d4b1f0864b765b3a0e6eaf5a62440e9a50a493","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/owner.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"43f48499256305c81642d0decec018ccd2d5734c316d1e9ac38c6ab8d1fdc9a0","body":{"detail":"After getToken() fails, ownerBrowser() retries with its own fetch of /api/token. When that succeeds the browser holds the events cookie, but api.ts's tokenPromise stays unset and its onToken listeners do not run, so the next getToken() fetches the token again, and the page's stream is reopened as the owner's only when the hub's next subscription on the old stream is refused (stream-hub.ts, unknown_stream) or a later getToken() succeeds. web/e2e/streams.spec.ts (the late-token test) shows the stream still reopening once.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":13},"end":{"line":15},"content_hash":"3583aab0722c57192d9777c50e3b423a5cb5f506f0d69f5340e6a13a39ff815d"},"suggested_fix":"Retry through getToken() (after its memo is dropped) so a success sets the memo and runs the onToken listeners.","summary":"ownerBrowser's own token retry leaves getToken's memo failed","supersedes":"5f5bc57859f2b885409663b911f557d29461631d62739169562fb16a9db8952d","tags":["review","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream-hub.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"0de6d056a59b5f7f7b32fc7cf91489ac31c28b777c80bf66c6323de42479a24c","body":{"detail":"The hub learns that the server carries /api/stream over a WebSocket only from a 426 to the plain request, and remembers it for its own life: once per shared worker, but once per page load where the hub runs in the tab (no SharedWorker). The daemon is unaffected. A server that advertised the transport (in the /a/ bootstrap, or a header on a response the shell already makes) would save the round trip on the time-to-usable path.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":342},"end":{"line":346},"content_hash":"e461307789815f4359eb9af3636cda0d5096499a69ff787f40b9ab7f66444374"},"summary":"On a Worker each new stream hub pays one 426 round trip before it opens the WebSocket","supersedes":"5870069c462f45753a3e950360e0868360aa8c04031b5c74a3593ea7d2478bcb","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream-hub.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:30:25.931134Z","id":"f7af5d6e1ba912cfadc116fa2e4533c0f7961d5edba9479cab37d1dd306ab6d8","body":{"detail":"drop() aborts the current connection. When that connection is a GET /api/stream whose response has not reached the page yet, Chrome keeps the socket to drain the response for reuse (about 5 s; the SSE body never ends) and only then closes it, so the daemon counts the stream as attached meanwhile (`open` and `levels` in GET /api/_test/stream/open), holding a second stream for the browser. The hub reopens at most once per caller change (the `reconnect` case compares the asked caller with the one the stream's `ready` named), so this happens when a reopen, a reconnect after a refused subscription, or a failure's retry lands while a connect is in flight. The daemon detaches a closed client within a millisecond; the delay is the browser's.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":547},"end":{"line":553},"content_hash":"50f43433859ae4b4960306f84d9917ae901ccd99c2692329e7e275099aa83ca7"},"suggested_fix":"Let an in-flight connect reach its `ready` before acting on a reconnect or a refused subscription (decide then, as an ask made while no stream is up already is), so the hub never aborts a stream request that has not answered.","summary":"A stream request aborted before it answers stays open on the daemon for up to 5 s","supersedes":"e604b4be66fabd7e5bc699b25d1e319d606f305badbf0c33b7c9a9d04c740b3c","tags":["risk","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/owner.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T12:31:12.224889Z","id":"7b5e30e3d8813988b144e1d294a7d0b33cc5bec04aba1314c219a3df56ab8907","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"50fbae8dc711f064037bc747aba83a54ee2a563dda7da6130d8f8ef2aed8dcad","summary":"Duplicate head left by a merge: the same record as 5f5bc57859f2b885409663b911f557d29461631d62739169562fb16a9db8952d (kept), re-anchored on a parallel branch. Proposed close: reason:duplicate.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/waiting.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T04:47:23.336895Z","id":"ecad42f2c2c91864e3508cc7d720dc3bb984777ece85fc34b395af113c311017","body":{"detail":"The daemon now reports state withheld with an approver name (crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs state_of) for a comment held from its agent until the agent's person approves its author; waitingLabel has no case for it, so the thread shows no waiting indicator. Spec §10 wants 'waiting for Sam's approval'. clax comments prints it (crates/clax-cli/src/commands/comments.rs delivery).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":35},"end":{"line":35},"content_hash":"94752ffd9323a0e85d941ed8b7de2099267ddbfee318f8338c4977428961c9be"},"summary":"The shell shows no delivery label for feedback_state withheld","supersedes":"b68a78ba03e7b2b67859cab95300df5a891e882c2852b57fb3b2752d4a23fce3","tags":["people","ui","spec:10","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/gallery.test.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T16:45:12.360131Z","id":"2147868f93039f2b025258026bd261e1fd75b93901a090a23e8ada5e7e2e0821","body":{"detail":"Failure: scripts/quality_gates.sh's web unit gate failed on this test with TypeError: from_html is not a function at shell/src/ui/GalleryCard.svelte:11, mounting Gallery after the test's own vi.resetModules() (line 451). A full ./node_modules/.bin/vitest run in web/ failed the same way once and passed once; the file alone passed three times; //web:unit under Bazel passed. A Svelte module evaluated half-way across a module reset is the likely cause; not confirmed. The test also waits 50 ms on the clock (line 457).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":444},"end":{"line":459},"content_hash":"12584fda52619295f7f1a8fe7673a8e3d8e3096f2985f220be7a30d17d1ffb5d"},"summary":"'shows People in the header to the owner and to a connected person, and not to a LAN viewer' fails now and then in a full vitest run: from_html is not a function","tags":["tests","flaky","web","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/waiting.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:02:35.345810Z","id":"6b3301dd44a48b7f9cbc91e047927896bf18750a0f9f13932d0295be2bd60988","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs:323 maps a sent thread on an `app` session to Tier::Wait, so feedback_state is {state: \"sent\", tier: \"wait\"} until the app's poll takes it. The comment at lines 3-8 says the daemon never emits `sent` with `wait`, and the label at line 13 says \"waiting on its wait_for_feedback loop\", an MCP tool the app's agent does not have (it long-polls GET /api/sessions/<sid>/feedback?tier=wait).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":3},"end":{"line":16},"content_hash":"dcd8af521919b3038e22fe84593dff81b0b40a4d78661b533af3babc8e233d52"},"suggested_fix":"Update the comment to say `sent`/`wait` is the app session's state, and word the `wait` label so it fits both an MCP wait_for_feedback call and the app's feedback poll (e.g. \"its feedback poll\").","summary":"Waiting labels: the comment says `sent` never names `wait`, which an app session now does","tags":["review","flutter-app","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/waiting.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T06:05:51.886249Z","id":"573ea2380d98b15d1cde6e7ad1cffa88557632927b3b3e183413bf73f07b258b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"The comment at web/shell/src/waiting.ts:3-9 now says `sent` names `wait` only for the Clax app's agent; the wait labels read \"its next feedback poll\" and \"its feedback poll\", naming no MCP tool. waiting.test.ts asserts the sent/wait label; `npx vitest run shell` (in web/): 85 files, 748 tests passed; `npm run typecheck`: 0 errors, 0 warnings.","supersedes":"6b3301dd44a48b7f9cbc91e047927896bf18750a0f9f13932d0295be2bd60988","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/artifact-main.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:22:41.152590Z","id":"3d52dac0442496e317390abd587c7d0eca21217f722e1adc92d967cea0414592","body":{"detail":"node web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs at commit 647958f22844: 'artifact: 64163 gzip bytes, over its budget of 64006'. The host module, its CSS and the attestation logic are a lazy chunk (host-*.js); the eager growth is the ?app=1 check and lazy import here, ArtifactMount.controller(), the controller's app hooks (welcome spread, posted call, location.search kept in here()/openPage), hostArrival in caps/gesture.ts, clax:scroll in BRIDGE_TYPES and the Composer's Send label. The extension composer grew 25621 -> 25648, inside its budget. web/perf/bundle-budget.json was left unchanged; its owner (plan Task W4) raises artifact by the measured growth.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":18},"end":{"line":18},"content_hash":"ec04f26eeba06549227d242fa50ec4dd2456686e6b8d50059983159aee6f7087"},"suggested_fix":"Raise bundle-budget.json's artifact to 64192 (64006 + 157 rounded up to 64) in Task W4.","summary":"Artifact bundle 64163 gzip bytes, 157 over its 64006 budget, from app mode's eager seams","tags":["budget","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/artifact-main.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:47:26.108085Z","id":"0c77e3ef5946471a07e520f38b9fa06384de04570bcf515234bcf0e0a40e01d5","body":{"detail":"node web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs: 'artifact: 64180 gzip bytes, over its budget of 64006' (appQuery in route.ts, shared by artifact-main.ts and the controller, plus the controller's gate/send now read by the host). Task W4 would set artifact to 64192 (64006 + 174 rounded up to 64).","kind":"comment","references":"3d52dac0442496e317390abd587c7d0eca21217f722e1adc92d967cea0414592","span":{"start":{"line":18},"end":{"line":18},"content_hash":"83ea6afa21706dca5b5e2a571adaf4900d27f6bf4e6125897ba3be30eaa30ddf"},"summary":"At 647958f22844 the artifact bundle is 64180 gzip bytes, 174 over 64006","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/artifact-main.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:47:43.015141Z","id":"353ae011b2982d1bde3974c250468f8028787583afdfaed72da1d8be20613d9c","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"3d52dac0442496e317390abd587c7d0eca21217f722e1adc92d967cea0414592","summary":"Correction to both budget figures above: 174 rounded up to a multiple of 64 is 192, so the artifact budget would be 64198 (64006 + 192), not 64192","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/artifact-main.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T10:19:10.697837Z","id":"f79dd36ed29c2d64c5451a7d1583d27f0ba21e122393dd300ab119a894a795c1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Budget raised to 64390 in 647958f22844. node web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs after a fresh scripts/build-web.sh: 'artifact 64370' with no budget exceeded, exit 0. Growth by task is in the comment on web/perf/bundle-budget.json:4:10.","supersedes":"3d52dac0442496e317390abd587c7d0eca21217f722e1adc92d967cea0414592","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T13:47:42.278198Z","id":"4ae443727226d20da2054a5b1e1b00927b9fbb9a7a61d97e8b374b4925b9f6fb","body":{"detail":"Failure: in the macOS debug app (apps/clax_app, flutter test -d macos driving AppRoot with the real daemon and WebViewAppSurface), open a made app, wait more than HIDDEN_MS (30 s), then comment and Send. The change lands in the store (version 2 published, agent reply posted, thread resolved, working.stop, all about 5 s after Send) but the shell posts no Landed and no further state: the app screen keeps 'Working…' and 'v1' for the full 7-minute wait. document.visibilityState in the app's WKWebView reads 'hidden' (hasFocus false) within a second of load and stays hidden, also after `osascript -e 'tell application id \"dev.empathic.clax\" to activate'` (whether the window was then frontmost was not confirmed). onVisibility then releases the non-background topics (artifact:<id>, working:<id>, docs:<id>) after HIDDEN_MS; only the background inbox topic stays, which is why /api/inbox/summary still refetched when the agent replied. Reproduced with no model: a replay backend returning recorded results with a 5 s delay lands when Send comes within 30 s of load (longpress-landed 5224 ms) and never lands when Send comes 40 s or 60 s after load. Seen first in a live claude -p run (artifact bmxd902nx4vm, thread 01M4R4P5AXWP3XXRE25B7YH5J4): no longpress-landed record was written. Whether a frontmost, unobscured app window also reports hidden is unverified; a window behind others does on macOS, and the change then waits until the page shows again.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":323},"end":{"line":342},"content_hash":"50c522e84cb5cdc1713ecbc3f861987420515d73d6fa24c51e8100ef15d8744e"},"suggested_fix":"In app mode (?app=1) take the page's visibility from the host (the Flutter AppLifecycleState, sent over window.claxHost) instead of document.visibilityState, or keep the artifact's own topics while hidden; and test that a change sent more than HIDDEN_MS after load lands in the macOS integration test (apps/clax_app/integration_test/full_loop_test.dart).","summary":"In the macOS app the page reports hidden, so 30 s after an app opens its shell drops the app's topics and a change that lands later never shows in place","tags":["live-run","app-mode","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T13:51:32.974316Z","id":"f44e53fbe7d2c52b425ec11515b7cd95e78f1ab3801db0e46fdc570f74e24695","body":{"kind":"comment","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","references":"4ae443727226d20da2054a5b1e1b00927b9fbb9a7a61d97e8b374b4925b9f6fb","summary":"App side done in f1c07f346b12: AppSurface.setVisible; the app screen reports shown while resumed or inactive with its route on top, hidden on hidden, paused or detached and under another route; ShellSession folds setVisible into each document's Init (after init, under the nonce) and sends a change only after init. Evidence: cd apps/clax_app && flutter test -> '+422 ~3: All tests passed!' (host_protocol_test.dart 'visibility is called only after init, and each Init carries it'; app_screen_test.dart 'the page is visible while the app is resumed and the screen on top'). Still needed before closing: the shell's claxHost.setVisible (web/shell/src/app/host.ts, uncommitted at f1c07f346b12) and the integration check that a change sent more than HIDDEN_MS after load lands (apps/clax_app/integration_test/full_loop_test.dart).","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T13:54:03.086272Z","id":"930c9c56e6a5d67332d7e30e71416908b2caa80923c8d012a96c516badf36ab2","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed: in app mode the shell takes visibility from the host (claxHost.setVisible; visible from init on), stream.ts reads it through visibility.hidden. Evidence: host.test.ts 'a hidden document does not stop the app's view following: a version 60 s later still lands' (test clock advanced 2 x HIDDEN_MS) and the setVisible tests pass, and fail with the host's rule removed; e2e/app-mode.spec.ts 'a version published after the hidden-page threshold still lands while the WebView reports the document hidden' (visibilityState forced hidden, shell clock advanced 60 s) passed 2/2; vitest 1546/1546. The macOS integration test is F10's to rerun.","supersedes":"4ae443727226d20da2054a5b1e1b00927b9fbb9a7a61d97e8b374b4925b9f6fb","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T13:58:38.843325Z","id":"9d5efeab752cdd8d3a6ba81d3326b8c1f8b0e8e2e00a4b6c7b2d5189344826bc","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"930c9c56e6a5d67332d7e30e71416908b2caa80923c8d012a96c516badf36ab2","summary":"Covered by apps/clax_app/integration_test/full_loop_test.dart since f1c07f346b12: the shell document reads visibilityState 'hidden' in the test's macOS WebView, the test waits until the shell's performance.now() passes 35 s (past HIDDEN_MS), then picks, comments and Sends; landed(2) arrives, the page shows the change with data and scroll kept, and one longpress-landed record for version 2 is written. Embedded clax rebuilt with 647958f22844 (just app-clax macos). Two runs: 00:39 +1 All tests passed, both. The release shell has no test clock, so the wait is real time. Not checked: the test failing against the pre-647958f22844 shell.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T14:15:38.577291Z","id":"efc2ce3c8ad3c302b2bf896c23628004fb839a710a50ba1cba27ee471bc68d51","body":{"detail":"Run log app a4w9vf5bgh6g (target/flutter-app/l1/run2): the new-app result was replayed from a recorded claude -p output, a run was added through the page, and the comment was sent with the shell's Send 47 s after load in a WebView that still reads document.visibilityState 'hidden'. The live claude -p change returned in 4.4 s; the shell posted Ready v2 and Landed v2; longpress-landed = 4846 ms; the thread was resolved; the run (runs/DnnqjVa49zPioAuWJTCW, 5.2 km, 1650 s) was kept and shows '5.20 km · 27:30 · 5:17/km'.","kind":"comment","references":"930c9c56e6a5d67332d7e30e71416908b2caa80923c8d012a96c516badf36ab2","span":{"start":{"line":323},"end":{"line":342},"content_hash":"164a9f1e4147eb9d26636e5d76f87d0200f47a00444601c3e22146c35da7b54b"},"summary":"Confirmed live at 647958f22844: a change sent 47 s after the app opened lands in place","tags":["live-run","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/visibility.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T14:34:42.909402Z","id":"dd6cb6ca6021b2d3a20b6c8359584105d45632e88d5f3dbc07e69df827598f0d","body":{"detail":"node web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs at 647958f22844 against a clean build of 647958f22844: artifact 64442 -> 64519 (budget 64512), gallery 27830 -> 27870, app host 3919 -> 3927, extension composer 25791 -> 25820. bundle-budget.json is unchanged.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":23},"end":{"line":23},"content_hash":"12734fe2ebbf6b56a8e510ec2f05392bd91eb000e691adca36f2cf2d4c36d184"},"suggested_fix":"Raise artifact to 64576 (64519 rounded up to 64).","summary":"Following the host's visibility in the consent dialog put the artifact bundle at 64519 gzip bytes, 7 over its 64512 budget","tags":["budget","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/visibility.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T14:35:11.585849Z","id":"9fe75d6f82d4baa23a7282cde6642d66f00ea3eb9e7121e73e65b4713d46ce35","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Artifact budget raised 64512 -> 64640 in 647958f22844 for 647958f22844's host-visibility arming. node web/scripts/bundle-size.mjs after a fresh scripts/build-web.sh: 'artifact 64519', exit 0.","supersedes":"dd6cb6ca6021b2d3a20b6c8359584105d45632e88d5f3dbc07e69df827598f0d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T14:10:17.212534Z","id":"312c4413312d729c8bc35c64beda47765c904b575b92abc393be45d5346b25a6","body":{"detail":"A tab hidden for HIDDEN_MS (30 s) releases its topics and fetches its state again when it shows; the shared connection has no per-tab resume point.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":336},"end":{"line":355},"content_hash":"11c6d5ee1beb1295890e20b19fe7e77227a5b2282068b40db1965fce57d3b24b"},"suggested_fix":"Per-topic rings in the worker would let a briefly hidden tab replay instead.","summary":"A hidden tab's catch-up is a refetch","supersedes":"0239b9e01e340c099e2641be35f6583631bb99281339a8f3de905ef92a9407ef","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-16T14:10:17.232708Z","id":"2704a06d5793040ee9842821ee13570cfb72b02af7227d1cc1f156d50d55c389","body":{"detail":"A tab counts its hub gone after DEAD_MS (35 s) without a ping, or at once where the browser fires close on the worker's port. A worker that lives but hangs is not restarted, since a new SharedWorker of the same name reaches the same instance. Leader tabs are not pinged at all: a hidden leader's timers are throttled and its followers would replace it needlessly; a leader hidden for 30 s leaves, so a frozen tab does not hold the connection for long.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":457},"end":{"line":460},"content_hash":"179f7bffd3ea769b233434bd4f135364ef246a4fcfac38935bbe0a93776dccb1"},"summary":"The shared worker is checked only by its pings; a hung worker is not restarted","supersedes":"87de9a6414227d430f6a7a7d5c5361145e613d37bac16d2064315c645579a079","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream-worker.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T22:01:59.714922Z","id":"82b23b84e3ad12874511ddd09d032c41e8d7f6a4f401062f4fe1f5b8867c9e6c","body":{"detail":"Seen 2026-10-17 in apps/clax_app/integration_test/full_loop_test.dart's second test (shell document hidden to WebKit from load): at the comment click (rig.comment, after the bridge loads clip-*.js), WebKit closed the worker's /api/stream connection and started a new worker instance that received a connect for the tab's open port, about 35 s after the worker started; it happened in most runs of that test, sometimes after the version 2 event had already arrived. Whether memory pressure, the clip's helper iframe, or WebKit's handling of hidden clients triggers it was not found. Since 647958f22844 the welcome makes the tab send its state again and the new hub opens a new stream whose `live` has the views refetch, so nothing is lost; a stream event that lands between the old instance's end and the new stream's subscription is recovered only by that refetch.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":26},"end":{"line":40},"content_hash":"a4022ef7e8bbab4ae308a993ed29fd7aaecf7241099cdb75962a6f3ec621b913"},"summary":"What makes WebKit end and relaunch the stream's shared worker in the Clax app on macOS is not known","tags":["webkit","macos","stream","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T22:03:21.265668Z","id":"b0c4991f49dd1e4b1c95a3f54e11bb0db4b3c44a75032c87110080dc250c76ab","body":{"detail":"Run log app a4w9vf5bgh6g (target/flutter-app/l1/run2): the new-app result was replayed from a recorded claude -p output, a run was added through the page, and the comment was sent with the shell's Send 47 s after load in a WebView that still reads document.visibilityState 'hidden'. The live claude -p change returned in 4.4 s; the shell posted Ready v2 and Landed v2; longpress-landed = 4846 ms; the thread was resolved; the run (runs/DnnqjVa49zPioAuWJTCW, 5.2 km, 1650 s) was kept and shows '5.20 km · 27:30 · 5:17/km'.","kind":"comment","references":"930c9c56e6a5d67332d7e30e71416908b2caa80923c8d012a96c516badf36ab2","span":{"start":{"line":347},"end":{"line":366},"content_hash":"164a9f1e4147eb9d26636e5d76f87d0200f47a00444601c3e22146c35da7b54b"},"summary":"Confirmed live at 647958f22844: a change sent 47 s after the app opened lands in place","supersedes":"efc2ce3c8ad3c302b2bf896c23628004fb839a710a50ba1cba27ee471bc68d51","tags":["live-run","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T22:03:21.278659Z","id":"d55e64195760aef209d6cb369b747a4ebf442e04ef2927f2b441676c5e3c6680","body":{"detail":"A tab hidden for HIDDEN_MS (30 s) releases its topics and fetches its state again when it shows; the shared connection has no per-tab resume point.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":360},"end":{"line":379},"content_hash":"11c6d5ee1beb1295890e20b19fe7e77227a5b2282068b40db1965fce57d3b24b"},"suggested_fix":"Per-topic rings in the worker would let a briefly hidden tab replay instead.","summary":"A hidden tab's catch-up is a refetch","supersedes":"312c4413312d729c8bc35c64beda47765c904b575b92abc393be45d5346b25a6","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T22:03:21.291405Z","id":"23e205f15ddcec6a371742f7ab534ac72882876296a062b0974d9cd4dd5b7163","body":{"detail":"A tab counts its hub gone after DEAD_MS (35 s) without a ping, or at once where the browser fires close on the worker's port. A worker that lives but hangs is not restarted, since a new SharedWorker of the same name reaches the same instance. Leader tabs are not pinged at all: a hidden leader's timers are throttled and its followers would replace it needlessly; a leader hidden for 30 s leaves, so a frozen tab does not hold the connection for long.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":481},"end":{"line":484},"content_hash":"179f7bffd3ea769b233434bd4f135364ef246a4fcfac38935bbe0a93776dccb1"},"summary":"The shared worker is checked only by its pings; a hung worker is not restarted","supersedes":"2704a06d5793040ee9842821ee13570cfb72b02af7227d1cc1f156d50d55c389","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream-hub.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T22:03:21.304176Z","id":"01855306804696538c10278736c341e4ab9f59455ac7efccfbf0ef159b63d35f","body":{"detail":"drop() aborts the current connection. When that connection is a GET /api/stream whose response has not reached the page yet, Chrome keeps the socket to drain the response for reuse (about 5 s; the SSE body never ends) and only then closes it, so the daemon counts the stream as attached meanwhile (`open` and `levels` in GET /api/_test/stream/open), holding a second stream for the browser. The hub reopens at most once per caller change (the `reconnect` case compares the asked caller with the one the stream's `ready` named), so this happens when a reopen, a reconnect after a refused subscription, or a failure's retry lands while a connect is in flight. The daemon detaches a closed client within a millisecond; the delay is the browser's.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":465},"end":{"line":471},"content_hash":"50f43433859ae4b4960306f84d9917ae901ccd99c2692329e7e275099aa83ca7"},"suggested_fix":"Let an in-flight connect reach its `ready` before acting on a reconnect or a refused subscription (decide then, as an ask made while no stream is up already is), so the hub never aborts a stream request that has not answered.","summary":"A stream request aborted before it answers stays open on the daemon for up to 5 s","supersedes":"8525f268fb8a05164766a18851d809e67ab80bd9ab2ce4b3200b0d7281681647","tags":["risk","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/transport.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:31:54.023179Z","id":"103360578ead774b6e8f5b658c1ae2924a067de3af06aa2c1196beb5dad96905","body":{"detail":"The stream hub sends Last-Event-ID on GET /api/stream (web/shell/src/stream-hub.ts:344); hostFetch drops the request's headers for /api/stream and posts only {type: \"subscribe\", id}, as docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md section 5.2 words the message. After a core reopen the hub therefore sees a new stream and refetches rather than replaying missed events. Carrying the header (or the lastEventId) in subscribe needs the host relay and the core subscription to accept it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":156},"end":{"line":176},"content_hash":"bb96d831294eee65b2e8558c1c9588bd5022f1c65c42bcc486e7eeceea5f22ad"},"summary":"subscribe {id} carries no Last-Event-ID: a stream reopened after streamEnd starts fresh instead of resuming","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/transport.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:31:54.023254Z","id":"f74fe86799a405c0091e8cca65d6647527694029c9b9c32e570e990ca104401c","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md section 5.1 gives call {id, method, path, headers, body, body64} and callChunk {id, n, last, body64} but not how the host tells a chunked call from an empty body. Here the call goes first with body and body64 null and chunked: true, then its chunks, n from 0, each its own base64 of CHUNK bytes; the host relays (web/e2e/app-host.ts, apps/clax_app's relay) must buffer until last before answering.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":120},"end":{"line":128},"content_hash":"68c6bf39856e8361d33f018cd9b6b5fe76af53f2b4ad0d9883444d05b59536f0"},"summary":"A chunked call is announced by chunked: true on its call message, a field the spec's call message does not name","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/gallery-main.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:31:54.023371Z","id":"7a588bda852bdc9aec6f6fa524fc6e0985bcfef6b365b2ebc0c5419c08f069ff","body":{"detail":"installTransport waits for channelNonce, which only claxHost.init calls, and installHost (web/shell/src/app/host.ts) installs claxHost only at /a/<id>?app=1. The app loads no other shell path today; a gallery shown in the app would hang on its first API call rather than fail.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":3},"end":{"line":7},"content_hash":"959a82cdb5c9bded4365568a02ee80bce5ddb1dda6b3d2e9f02abd5bb15913e8"},"summary":"In app mode the gallery replaces fetch, but only the artifact view installs claxHost, so its API calls would wait forever for a nonce","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/transport.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:48:02.574537Z","id":"b92e8b99ae0ebef79f6805ed99d82e7a39d48fd944234e0fb10707eeb2ee2b71","body":{"detail":"hostFetch checks signal.aborted before and after `await link.ready` (lines 115, 119) and subscribe() after its own (line 158), but listens for abort only once the call is posted. docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md section 5.1 says an aborted signal rejects with an AbortError. A vitest probe with `ready: new Promise(() => {})`, a call to /api/x, then ac.abort(): after 50 ms the promise is still pending; the same for /api/stream. lifecycle.ts retrying() awaits the attempt, so its STUCK_MS abort and a Lifecycle dispose do not end an attempt made before init; in the gallery (record 7a588bda) nothing ever does. transport.test.ts's 'aborts' case aborts only after the call is posted.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":113},"end":{"line":119},"content_hash":"47b7f4c3c805f5b7506059a46527ebfa8f832d354173178cfb757eeb72ffd368"},"suggested_fix":"Race link.ready (and the body read) against the signal's abort event, rejecting with abortError(signal) and posting nothing; add the probe above as a test for both a call and the stream.","summary":"An aborted signal does not reject a call or a stream made before init: it stays pending until the nonce comes, forever where none does","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/transport.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:48:02.574578Z","id":"31f23b836d794abaf0375256e20b171ec0090e20bd119fbbfd96b62eb913a3be","body":{"detail":"calls, streams and lastId (lines 72-74) are per document and start at 1, and callResult/streamBlock/streamEnd take only the ID. When the shell document reloads (a reload, reloadLatest, a navigation to another version), the app's runJavaScript reaches the new document; an answer to the old load's call 3 resolves the new load's call 3 with another request's response, and an old subscription's blocks feed the new stream 1. The nonce (app/host.ts header, transport.ts installTransport) checks only messages the shell posts. docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-19-in-process-core.md Task 15's ChannelRelay says dispose drops pending answers but not that answers are bound to the load whose nonce the call carried.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":179},"end":{"line":207},"content_hash":"cc7c387ceb7fd4c8d7e104f5907b8e21967418df581f4a2fd9031e8bdab2802a"},"suggested_fix":"Give callResult, streamBlock and streamEnd the call's nonce and drop an answer whose nonce is not this load's (or make the relay drop answers across loads and pin it in channel_relay_test.dart), with a transport test of a mismatched answer.","summary":"Answers carry no load: IDs restart at 1 in every document, so a late callResult or streamBlock from the previous load lands on the new document's call or stream","tags":["review","security","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/transport.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:48:02.574612Z","id":"0774f920d26a7ac5fc23034740ad1ecf9b02550e8209332e885e216f8eba17b6","body":{"detail":"installTransport's ready is the nonce from claxHost.init. The app calls init from _onLoaded on onPageFinished (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/webview_surface.dart:167-170), and Init's script polls every 50 ms for window.claxHost (apps/clax_app/lib/ui/host_protocol.dart:883-891), which exists only once app/host's chunk has loaded. A document's load event waits for its iframes, so threads, presence, the stream and every capability call a page makes through the shell's bridge (a page reading its db at start) wait for the page itself to finish loading. On the daemon they went out at once. Section 5.1 of docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md asks for the wait; section 4.4 makes the main-frame and origin filter the first check and the nonce a second. Not measured in a running app.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":224},"end":{"line":241},"content_hash":"8436e717cc016396634fb18e5761ab4cd5cf927374cca9bed2252d1d266f2cf0"},"suggested_fix":"Have the app's scheme handler write a fresh per-load nonce into the shell document it answers (beside the clax-embed meta), so the transport posts from boot; or let the channel's first check alone admit calls until init.","summary":"In app mode every shell API call waits for the app's init, which comes after the shell document's load event, so after the artifact page's full load and the lazy host chunk","tags":["review","perf","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/lifecycle.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:48:02.574647Z","id":"80f50481a4a57399f9c099d4ffeadde3c7f2a80d1bb35cf1d43d3bb2efd65156","body":{"detail":"The only trouble callbacks are connTrouble calls (web/shell/src/ui/Gallery.svelte:83, web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts:807), and connTrouble shows nothing while notices are off. Dropping the check measured gallery 28081 to 28053 and artifact 66215 to 66187 in a build where the transport is a dynamic import.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":100},"end":{"line":103},"content_hash":"dc97b415635d737e34cbba9637038b13f1597c129a329ee27050d59f13e06e81"},"suggested_fix":"Keep retrying generic and let the notice decide what shows; move the 'reports no trouble' test to conn-notice.test.ts.","summary":"retrying's connNoticesOn check repeats what connNotices(false) already does, ties lifecycle.ts to the notice module, and costs 28 gzip bytes in each browser entry","tags":["review","perf","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/transport.test.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:48:02.574684Z","id":"24d172de64a170f933ad1af1a36a6d46cba452ec7ee0b98ad7b9c0c90a30171b","body":{"detail":"'chunks a body over the limit' counts nine callChunk messages and checks the last one's flag; it does not decode each body64 against its slice, check n from 0 in order, the call's chunked: true or its null body and body64. No test aborts a call or a stream before init (both stay pending, see the concern on lines 113-119), aborts an open stream (the stop() and c.error path in subscribe), or answers a 204 or a malformed result (NULL_BODY, callResult's catch).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":42},"end":{"line":75},"content_hash":"8bb8c4da35bd89bb4b30e8ac74cbb7afb72897762069ee85ec5bc32163e10cf3"},"summary":"The chunking, abort and stream tests pin counts and ends, not contents: no test reassembles the chunks, checks chunked: true, aborts before init or aborts a stream","tags":["review","test-gap","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/gallery-main.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:48:02.575161Z","id":"3d95dc9a18cb5b0d1d375f11a1ab4f30d16785d614590f48303e1c5d29816278","body":{"detail":"callResult, streamBlock and streamEnd exist only as methods of the claxHost object installHost defines (web/shell/src/app/host.ts), which only /a/<id> with app=1 loads, so a gallery given a nonce would still never hear an answer. The app's Init script gives up after waitMs (10 s, apps/clax_app/lib/ui/host_protocol.dart:860-891) when no claxHost appears. An artifact document in app mode without app=1 in its query installs the transport and no host, with the same result.","kind":"comment","references":"7a588bda852bdc9aec6f6fa524fc6e0985bcfef6b365b2ebc0c5419c08f069ff","span":{"start":{"line":3},"end":{"line":7},"content_hash":"959a82cdb5c9bded4365568a02ee80bce5ddb1dda6b3d2e9f02abd5bb15913e8"},"suggested_fix":"Let the transport own its receivers in every app-mode document (window.claxTransport with init, callResult, streamBlock, streamEnd, as the bundle plan on web/perf/bundle-budget.json:3:7 option (1)A has it), and fail calls with a TypeError rather than wait when no init can come.","summary":"Confirmed, and wider: the answers have nowhere to land either, and the artifact entry without app=1 hangs the same way","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/transport.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:48:02.575443Z","id":"b311f7a991e16bf0497f4901926fe19715fad53f5f6cf84c516639c388fe1ad8","body":{"detail":"web/shell/src/stream-hub.ts:344 sets Last-Event-ID (and line 378 the last_event_id query); subscribe() in transport.ts drops the request's headers and query. docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md section 2.4 has clax_embed_subscribe send GET /api/stream with nothing to resume from. Either the spec's subscribe gains lastEventId (shell, relay and core), or section 5.2 says a reopen refetches.","kind":"comment","references":"103360578ead774b6e8f5b658c1ae2924a067de3af06aa2c1196beb5dad96905","span":{"start":{"line":156},"end":{"line":176},"content_hash":"bb96d831294eee65b2e8558c1c9588bd5022f1c65c42bcc486e7eeceea5f22ad"},"summary":"Confirmed, and the spec contradicts itself here: section 5.2 says the hub resumes with Last-Event-ID, while its subscribe message and section 2.4's subscription carry no resume point","tags":["review","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/transport.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:57:37.105985Z","id":"80018c29f0f7c74bb2e54b0704121d72944569aad686876cf9320bbb489e5a0b","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"0774f920d26a7ac5fc23034740ad1ecf9b02550e8209332e885e216f8eba17b6","summary":"The owner chose this path on 2026-10-19: transport.js written by the core (option (1)A), boxOf in app/host.ts, no `at` in the bridge with the app's composer placed from the shell's anchors answer, the inspect view's handlers in a chunk, answers bound to the load's nonce, the nonce in the document, and subscribe carrying lastEventId.","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
