{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/gallery-main.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:57:37.672046Z","id":"2961bdf3fbfb0350b26dab03b93d20915af74fbe43782f64007aa93c25423cb4","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed by 647958f22844: every shell document the core marks loads transport.js, which installs its own window.claxTransport receivers. Evidence: transport.test.ts 'in app mode gives any shell document its own receivers…' (no claxHost) passes in bazelisk test //web:unit.","supersedes":"7a588bda852bdc9aec6f6fa524fc6e0985bcfef6b365b2ebc0c5419c08f069ff","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/lifecycle.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:57:37.896045Z","id":"428e81e310dda0c2c67d5b62c984af738573ec179c2bc5bbdaec0e2aa213fa1b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed by 647958f22844: lifecycle.ts and conn-notice.ts are as at 647958f22844^; the transport hides .conn-notice with its own style. bazelisk test //web:unit passes.","supersedes":"80f50481a4a57399f9c099d4ffeadde3c7f2a80d1bb35cf1d43d3bb2efd65156","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/transport.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:57:38.092944Z","id":"42d864f8530398634da9ac47fc4e3ab37f2ced240b7240f8a039bc50c8f20fde","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed by 647958f22844: the wait for the nonce races the signal. 'rejects a call and a stream aborted before init, and posts neither' timed out before and passes after (bazelisk test //web:unit --test_arg=shell/src/transport.test.ts).","supersedes":"b92e8b99ae0ebef79f6805ed99d82e7a39d48fd944234e0fb10707eeb2ee2b71","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/transport.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:57:38.306408Z","id":"ae230d26baa39c424d1b29e176806b949751bc089e4556aeae7ae7b9c6b5f6eb","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed by 647958f22844: callResult, streamBlock and streamEnd take the nonce first and drop another's. 'drops a late answer from an old load that names an ID the new load uses too' passes, and fails (event: old delivered) with the nonce check removed.","supersedes":"31f23b836d794abaf0375256e20b171ec0090e20bd119fbbfd96b62eb913a3be","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/transport.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:57:38.463375Z","id":"b16d43d0613c402d3e902ebd8c0970ada01d0aba65121ee933990eb5ac91bac3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Decided and done on the shell's side by 647958f22844: the transport reads <meta name=\"clax-nonce\"> and posts from boot ('posts from boot under the nonce the app wrote into the document, and ignores init' passes); spec sections 4.4/5.1 and plan Task 15 (647958f22844) have the scheme handler write it, init the fallback until then.","supersedes":"0774f920d26a7ac5fc23034740ad1ecf9b02550e8209332e885e216f8eba17b6","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/transport.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:57:38.676214Z","id":"f948c4df11c6abce428af784653e1433e743709c003707bf2671716b6b90e3c2","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Decided; the shell's half by 647958f22844 (subscribe {id, lastEventId} from Last-Event-ID or last_event_id; 'subscribes from the stream's resume point…' passes), spec 2.4/5.2 agree since 647958f22844. The core's half is the concern on crates/clax-embed/src/events.rs:30, left to plan Task 15.","supersedes":"103360578ead774b6e8f5b658c1ae2924a067de3af06aa2c1196beb5dad96905","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/transport.test.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:57:38.795691Z","id":"ec35309af968bc9ed0fe74fce8e1ee71bc1ff8e2719cc006dd8b18d793a72caf","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f22844","summary":"Fixed by 647958f22844 and 647958f22844: chunks decoded against their slices with n in order and chunked: true, abort before init (call and stream), abort of an open stream, a 204 with a body, malformed results. Each content test fails with its behaviour mutated (chunked flag, NULL_BODY, c.error) and passes as built.","supersedes":"24d172de64a170f933ad1af1a36a6d46cba452ec7ee0b98ad7b9c0c90a30171b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream-hub.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T09:32:18.755959Z","id":"786143fc75335061f315a1a4564d7b1f377597351e706d0509a4467c9fa9f720","body":{"detail":"With HubEnv.host, fail() opens the stream again at once (no backoff, no failure count), as docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md section 5.2 asks: the host owns liveness. run() fails on any answer that is not OK and on any end of the body, so a host that answers GET /api/stream with an error, or pushes streamEnd right after each subscribe (a core shutting down, a refused subscription), makes the hub post subscribe again for as long as some tab wants a topic. Each round is one channel round trip, so the page stays responsive, but the host and the core spend work on it. Pinned by web/shell/src/stream-hub.test.ts 'opens the stream again at once when it ends' (three ends, three reopens).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":570},"end":{"line":576},"content_hash":"3701efe051ae4f838a6b693e37ec65dff9b37913cdf764b92cb17db3f5f9dd66"},"suggested_fix":"If it shows in practice: on the host, reopen at once after an end that followed a ready, and wait for the host's next word (or one backoff step) after an answer that is not OK or an end with no ready.","summary":"On the app's host a stream the host refuses or ends at once is asked for again at once, with no backoff: a loop paced only by the channel's round trip","tags":["app","stream","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream-hub.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T09:52:53.542762Z","id":"8ccf6f0762a188cce497cc62a3bcf6b1d6e00d8f0d588e92a6bc28d14f2e5069","body":{"detail":"Three facts make the unpaced reopen worse than the record says. (1) The hub cannot see a refusal: web/shell/src/transport.ts subscribe() answers GET /api/stream 200 before the host has subscribed, so the core's status reaches the page only as the closing `event: end` block, which the hub's frame() ignores (its data has no topic), and docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md §5.2 (lines 693-707) does not say the host passes that block through streamBlock at all. (2) A second loop: subscribe() (stream-hub.ts, `if (res.status >= 500) { this.fail(); ... }`) calls fail(), which on the host reconnects at once, the new ready flushes the same POST, and a core that answers it 5xx is asked again per round trip, end block or not. (3) The spec contradicts itself: §2.4 (lines 355-385) says each consumer, the WebView's shell document named among them, stops for good on stream_refused 400/403/404 and on core_closed/core_failed and resubscribes after any other end with the stream's backoff, as apps/clax_app/lib/core/core_transport.dart sse() does (_final = {400, 403, 404}, 0.5 s doubling to 30 s); §5.2 says the host-mode hub has no backoff and reopens 'as after any end'. A shell document cannot see the core reopen, so stopping on core_closed/core_failed would leave it dead until reload: retrying those with the capped backoff heals itself. Stopping on a final refusal means leaving conn null with no retry timer, so Hub.changed() opens the stream again when a tab's topics change, as a refused topic is asked again (`retry`). Paced reopens keep what §5.2 is for: no connect, idle or subscription timeout and no stream_down, since a silent stream is never failed on the host. The other way, the host owning the WebView's resubscription itself (a CoreTransport.sse-style loop behind one page stream, streamEnd only when final), keeps the hub passive but makes the host parse and re-encode SSE and track the resume point the hub already holds.","kind":"comment","references":"786143fc75335061f315a1a4564d7b1f377597351e706d0509a4467c9fa9f720","suggested_fix":"stream-hub.ts: in run(), remember the `end` block's {reason, status} on this connection (frame() is skipped for it); in fail() on the host: if the last end was stream_refused with 400, 403 or 404, drop and return (no retry timer); otherwise drop and `this.retry = setTimeout(() => { this.retry = undefined; if (this.wanted().size) this.connect(); }, backoff(this.failures++))`, telling no tab; in run() skip the /api/token request when env.host (failures is now non-zero there). Tests in stream-hub.test.ts with host: true: three ends with no ready reopen after growing waits (none before backoff(0)'s floor of 400 ms); an end after a ready reopens after one short wait and resumes from Last-Event-ID; an end block {reason: stream_refused, status: 403} opens nothing in 10 minutes of fake time, and a topics message then opens one stream; a POST answered 503 reopens after a backoff, not at once; no status message and no /api/token in any. Spec §5.2: the host passes every block of the core's subscription, the closing `event: end` included, by streamBlock, then calls streamEnd; replace 'and no backoff' / 'as after any end' with this policy; §2.4: say shell documents retry core_closed and core_failed with the backoff, since only the host sees the core reopen.","summary":"Proposed host-mode policy: stop on a final refusal (stream_refused 400/403/404) until a tab's topics change; after any other end, and after a 5xx on POST /api/stream/<id>, reopen after the stream's backoff (lifecycle.ts backoff, 0.5 s doubling to 30 s, reset by ready), with no status and no /api/token; the spec's §2.4 and §5.2 disagree today","tags":["review","app","stream","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream-hub.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T09:52:53.542853Z","id":"5e11d403f6fc0e20cc0c3763f973f13f9d8101b45cd4a81c76bf194be1f79651","body":{"detail":"localLink (web/shell/src/stream.ts:210-214) never sends hello with a lock, so its one client is unlocked, and ping() detaches an unlocked client not heard for CLIENT_TTL_MS (180 s). Answers to pings run on the page's own timers, so when the WebView is suspended (iOS backgrounding, Android pausing timers) and Date.now() moves on, the first PING_MS interval after the wake detaches 'self' before sending its ping; changed() then starts the LINGER_MS close, the stream is aborted (transport unsubscribe), and EventStream is told nothing: a link without `pinged` has no watchdog. The artifact view keeps its topics unless it navigates, so it stops following comments and versions with no notice, which the app hides anyway (§5.2 says a hidden WebView keeps its subscription). Reproduced by a probe test: a Hub with host: true whose tab answers pings, topics ['gallery'], 30 s of timers, then vi.setSystemTime(+10 min) and PING_MS + 5 s of timers: stats().topics is [] and connected is false. The host hub also keeps the STUCK_MS (8 s) abort in getJson for the inbox baseline and catch-up, a timer §5.2's 'no timeouts' does not mention.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":275},"end":{"line":281},"content_hash":"dddf8fb57d26d6f63d7f58b8f5c8f874acd14f8be006dbfc142df47d2c722042"},"suggested_fix":"A local hub lives and dies with its one tab: have localLink send {t: 'hello', lock: 'self'} and give its Hub watchLock: () => {} so the client is locked and never expires (in a browser too), or skip the pinger altogether on env.host, where no link watches pings. Test: the probe above, asserting topics ['gallery'] and connected true after the jump. Decide whether getJson's STUCK_MS stays on the host and say so in §5.2.","summary":"On the app's host the in-tab hub expires its own tab after a WebView suspension longer than CLIENT_TTL_MS, closing the stream while the page still believes its topics live","tags":["review","app","stream","major","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/transport.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T09:52:53.542904Z","id":"8f19db9f2a41a674aaedf7f127b09f49b20cbe803c9efe7e061c1f09a472cee4","body":{"detail":"Object.freeze is shallow, so `claxTransport.embed.content = …` changes what web/shell/src/origin.ts artifactOrigin and web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts decideOrigin answer from then on, and with them the frameOrigin that web/shell/src/bridge-link.ts acceptFromFrame trusts. No page can reach it (a page is another origin and claxTransport is defined non-writable and non-configurable before the shell's modules run), so this is robustness, not a hole; putting the embed on claxTransport is sound, since transport.js is a classic script of its own and the window is the one place the shell's modules can read it without the meta's parser.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":304},"end":{"line":304},"content_hash":"621e79198c01868613485c69dbbcc94958e41e46f4dfcf8650ef6b09f1c8f62b"},"suggested_fix":"`Object.freeze({ ...receivers, embed: Object.freeze(embed) })`, and in transport.test.ts installTransport's app-mode case assert Object.isFrozen(hostEmbed(win)).","summary":"claxTransport is frozen but its embed is not: the origins every artifact frame is checked against can be rewritten by any shell code","tags":["review","app","minor","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/api-image.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T09:52:53.543004Z","id":"bd5b0535b8592071a742e524ffa680319f0c92eaf69032a1e39cd2fd7406feba","body":{"detail":"apiImageSrc keeps one object URL per path in a module-wide map for the document's life. Clip.svelte loads only near the view (IntersectionObserver, 200px margin), so what is held is the clips seen, each at most clax_core::clips::MAX_BYTES (5 MiB, crates/clax-core/src/clips.rs:27); a long session on an artifact with many large clips keeps them all in the WebView's memory, and a deleted thread's blob stays too. Revoking when the thumbnail unmounts would break the enlarged view only if the same URL were reused later, which a reference count covers. The only /api/ image the shell points at is this clip (ThreadCard.svelte:160); no gallery surface shows clips, and the app loads no gallery documents.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":8},"end":{"line":24},"content_hash":"5e39a1ca1f6321fd8d264ceacdca226939312e11e36b710ba1f1298d6d8f61b7"},"suggested_fix":"If memory shows in practice: a reference count per path (acquire in Clip's load, release on its destroy) that revokes at zero, or an LRU of about 32 entries that revokes what it evicts.","summary":"Clip object URLs are never revoked: an artifact view holds every clip it has scrolled near, up to 5 MiB each, until the document goes","tags":["review","app","minor","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream-hub.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T10:44:55.814769Z","id":"82dde54c1ef4ca17b2933e37fb514f1c8fc7b6abcdffd203708da94b359345e4","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"8ccf6f0762a188cce497cc62a3bcf6b1d6e00d8f0d588e92a6bc28d14f2e5069","summary":"Owner's decision (2026-10-20): the reply's policy. The host forwards every block of the core's subscription, the closing event: end included, then calls streamEnd; the hub stops on a final refusal (stream_refused 400/403/404) and reopens when a tab's topics change; after any other end, or a 5xx on POST /api/stream/<id>, it reopens after backoff(failures++), reset by ready; no status and no /api/token on the host; no connect, idle or subscription timeout.","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream-hub.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T10:44:55.815240Z","id":"d32aa57864a1021c00fa4b011aa91b92db81c22e8f8b408172327890df22f54e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f2284459b2440c3504082626f77bdacfae","summary":"Fixed as decided (8ccf6f07, owner 2026-10-20): web/shell/src/stream-hub.ts fail() reads the end block's {reason, status}, stops on stream_refused 400/403/404 and otherwise reopens after backoff(failures++); run() skips /api/token on the host. Spec 2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md §2.4 and §5.2 state the policy; plan Task 15's relay forwards the end block. bazelisk test //web:unit passed, with stream-hub.test.ts's host cases: growing waits after ends with no ready, one short wait and Last-Event-ID after a ready, nothing in 10 minutes after stream_refused 400, 403 and 404 then one stream on a topics change, a backoff after stream_refused 503 and after a 503 subscription answer, no status and no /api/token.","supersedes":"786143fc75335061f315a1a4564d7b1f377597351e706d0509a4467c9fa9f720","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream-hub.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T10:44:55.996528Z","id":"1c6b4ff24103c1f7ba5d01ef1095066fafb151a4f18cd6570c3d1b10c76c3a33","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f2284459b2440c3504082626f77bdacfae","summary":"Fixed: web/shell/src/stream.ts localLink sends {t: 'hello', lock: 'self'} to a Hub whose watchLock never fires, so its one tab is never expired (in a browser's local fallback too); getJson sets no STUCK_MS abort on the host; spec §5.2 says both. bazelisk test //web:unit passed with stream.test.ts 'keeps the page's topics through a suspension longer than a tab's expiry' (30 s, a 10-minute clock jump, PING_MS + 5 s: one stream, not aborted) and stream-hub.test.ts 'waits on an inbox request that does not answer' (10 minutes, no abort); both failed before the fix.","supersedes":"5e11d403f6fc0e20cc0c3763f973f13f9d8101b45cd4a81c76bf194be1f79651","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/transport.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T10:44:56.170212Z","id":"2e8ff1d8afa23bba0eb73faad657d3a4d9a6b61fdee27e4ee5bcdd974b2e0aa8","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f2284459b2440c3504082626f77bdacfae","summary":"Fixed: installTransport freezes embed with the receivers. bazelisk test //web:unit passed with transport.test.ts's app-mode case asserting Object.isFrozen(win.claxTransport) and Object.isFrozen(hostEmbed(win)) (failed before); //web:bundle_size passed, transport 2022 gzip bytes of its 2038 budget.","supersedes":"8f19db9f2a41a674aaedf7f127b09f49b20cbe803c9efe7e061c1f09a472cee4","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/api-image.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T10:44:56.371670Z","id":"86910c30ec9021cac52b6bec4ed1ef582e6460d3969c5ded16d2558a028a612d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:647958f2284459b2440c3504082626f77bdacfae","summary":"Fixed: apiImageSrc keeps the CLIPS_KEPT (32) most recently asked-for object URLs and revokes each one it evicts; an evicted clip is fetched again when asked for. bazelisk test //web:unit passed with api-image.test.ts 'keeps the most recent clips and revokes each one it lets go' (failed before).","supersedes":"bd5b0535b8592071a742e524ffa680319f0c92eaf69032a1e39cd2fd7406feba","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream-hub.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T02:52:29.357038Z","id":"591dd598171597ad24d8134b412f6706bdfc23a4f5c7fa9b67c646dcdbadc70a","body":{"detail":"Failure: in app mode (Hub env.host), a topic whose POST /api/stream/<id> the core answers 503 on every try. Each reopen's ready sets this.failures = 0 (stream-hub.ts:463), then the subscription answers 503 and fail() backs off from the first step again, so the backoff never grows and the stream reopens at the first step's wait indefinitely. web/shell/src/stream-hub.test.ts:731 (\"opens the stream again after a backoff, not at once, when a subscription answers 503\") pins the first wait only, and spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md:771 (\"`ready` resets the backoff\") produces this loop. A related case: a subscription answered unknown_stream (stream-hub.ts:704-709) calls connect() at once with no backoff, so a core that keeps answering it is asked in a tight loop on the host.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":462},"end":{"line":463},"content_hash":"0b7fdb9c4179ada304e7bad84c915bd4fdc134f37f65067ba2c44bb3565a4d25"},"suggested_fix":"Reset failures only when a subscription succeeds (the POST answers 2xx), not at ready, and give the unknown_stream reconnect the same backoff; amend spec 5.2's wording to match. Add a unit case: a subscription answering 503 every time waits longer on each reopen.","summary":"On the app's host a subscription the core keeps answering 5xx reopens the stream about every 0.5 s forever: ready resets failures before the subscription is asked","tags":["status:needs-decision","review","app-mode","stream","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/transport.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T02:52:29.357115Z","id":"86d55dcba9014cec418c47677f3f748eb413fb0e4e4b6a6d82825a073b22579b","body":{"detail":"A shell document without a well-formed clax-nonce meta waits for claxTransport.init (transport.ts:24-28, :262-267). The only documents without the meta were the app's over loopback, which the in-process core retires; the scheme handlers write the meta into every shell document they serve (transport.ts:24-26). Keeping init means an init the app queued for a previous load can still give a new meta-less document the old load's nonce. The e2e stand-in keeps this path alive with nonceMeta: false (web/e2e/app-scheme.ts:36, :371, :411, :479; web/e2e/app-transport.spec.ts:392).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":262},"end":{"line":267},"content_hash":"55339cab8bbd755abcd7c89c1843fa4eb8d7b01d795374533de1498c6001b1eb"},"suggested_fix":"Keep init in the frozen claxTransport object as a no-op (the app may still call it), treat a document without a well-formed clax-nonce meta as having no channel (calls and streams reject at once with TypeError(\"no app channel\"), as transport.ts now does without window.ClaxHost), drop the loopback wording in the header, and retire nonceMeta: false from the stand-in and its tests.","summary":"The claxTransport.init fallback serves only the retired loopback app and keeps a stale-init hazard","tags":["status:needs-decision","review","app-mode","transport","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/socket-url.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-21T02:52:29.357187Z","id":"73c4d74bc7402a867ccebeaa35a8e37c23d9865670326ef7d0b57480f8f17d3d","body":{"detail":"socketUrl answers wss: for an https: origin, ws: for an http: origin, and null in the app (onHost) or on any other scheme. A strict reading of \"build only wss:\" would also refuse ws: in the browser, which breaks the room capability and the live layers for the loopback daemon (http://localhost:7480) and LAN viewers (http://<lan-ip>:7480), whose routes are served over plain HTTP (crates/clax-server/src/router.rs:579-589). The rule in docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md section 4 covers app platforms only, so ws: is kept for the browser.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":7},"end":{"line":10},"content_hash":"6ad56a7fe8ded27cf935b677897289db895be69fc5db08c06fc84f2d09e46c7b"},"suggested_fix":"Owner to confirm the browser keeps ws: on a plain-http daemon, or say that browser rooms and live layers should require https.","summary":"socketUrl still builds ws: on a browser's plain-http daemon; only the app and unknown schemes get no socket","tags":["status:needs-decision","design","websocket","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/theme.css","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:34:19.533675Z","id":"28a748069435a3ff57dd6f38979a1bece60c87ed93390f01685a6791a58421f3","body":{"detail":"A card's tags are buttons, which its link may not hold, so they sit over the link's third row (.ctags), sized by a grid the link shares through grid-template-rows: subgrid. Browsers without subgrid (Chrome before 117, Safari before 16, Firefox before 71) would draw the tags over the card's footer.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":135},"end":{"line":142},"content_hash":"86492df0f65abb54a1a0729e7284e4e98e6a7aa5d069db5cffd7abb35ef99646"},"summary":"Gallery cards lay out their tags with CSS subgrid","tags":["tags","browsers","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/gallery.test.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:11:01.582622Z","id":"39199775920fd7b9f4a896f3da3aeda15435dfd1c770aa5d0c352545524a4975","body":{"detail":"Failure: scripts/quality_gates.sh's web unit gate failed on this test with TypeError: from_html is not a function at shell/src/ui/GalleryCard.svelte:11, mounting Gallery after the test's own vi.resetModules() (line 451). A full ./node_modules/.bin/vitest run in web/ failed the same way once and passed once; the file alone passed three times; //web:unit under Bazel passed. A Svelte module evaluated half-way across a module reset is the likely cause; not confirmed. The test also waits 50 ms on the clock (line 457).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":446},"end":{"line":461},"content_hash":"12584fda52619295f7f1a8fe7673a8e3d8e3096f2985f220be7a30d17d1ffb5d"},"summary":"'shows People in the header to the owner and to a connected person, and not to a LAN viewer' fails now and then in a full vitest run: from_html is not a function","supersedes":"2147868f93039f2b025258026bd261e1fd75b93901a090a23e8ada5e7e2e0821","tags":["tests","flaky","web","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/gallery.test.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T15:34:57.685881Z","id":"89496e501de45ac9ff68c343430d0be04466dc9c1a64995449fdf24a68658ddf","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:41837996d","summary":"Fixed: a lazy chunk of the previous gallery still evaluating across the mid-test vi.resetModules() loaded the Svelte runtime into the new registry half-evaluated. The test now awaits freshModules() (vi.dynamicImportSettled() then the reset). bazelisk test //web:unit --runs_per_test=10 --nocache_test_results on a machine at load average ~90: 10/10 'Test Files 180 passed (180)', no from_html; before the fix, 6 runs under the same load plus 8 busy loops reproduced it once.","supersedes":"39199775920fd7b9f4a896f3da3aeda15435dfd1c770aa5d0c352545524a4975","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:d1f51555-8e8f-4c11-acd6-673f773ac34d"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/topbar.test.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T10:40:08.590631Z","id":"83199b33b15443561c5644cc4b67af9a8d998bc5ad3599d5b80ed7b64c14ed2a","body":{"detail":"\"sidebar has no composer when comments off\" (line 299) and \"Get in Clax shows only for apps\" (line 315) sleep 50 ms before expecting .new-comment-open and a.get-in-clax to be absent. Under load the lazy chunk may not have loaded by then, so the checks can pass without checking (the same pattern record 9cef5716 notes in artifact-controller.test.ts). AGENTS.md forbids sleeps standing in for a condition.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":299},"end":{"line":315},"content_hash":"1f70dfca59511de81d242729abd000f6d2cf696b80a37b214d2705fbea1b5e5f"},"suggested_fix":"Wait for the event that ends the window (vi.dynamicImportSettled(), or the Share/Fork island that loads in the same pass) before the negative assertion.","summary":"Two of the new Comments-switch tests wait 50 ms and then assert that something did not appear","tags":["app-push","tests","review","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/topbar.test.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T11:06:47.632746Z","id":"ad98749d1e31086d884f9bb9426a422824f5c7a55eeabae30a5f3f690ae60b5d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:6fb64b9d4","summary":"Both 50 ms sleeps are replaced by await vi.dynamicImportSettled() and a flush before the negative assertions. just web-test: //web:unit, typecheck, lint, bundle_size PASSED; just test-affected d523321fd: 111 tests pass (target/t6b.log). ","supersedes":"83199b33b15443561c5644cc4b67af9a8d998bc5ad3599d5b80ed7b64c14ed2a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/theme.css","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T19:18:59.099166Z","id":"f91181cad8e92c71e0a83ef104fb45d9eb260b09491ace1b5055ec23f8fdfa84","body":{"detail":"The phone rule hides .ttl .by, the line web/shell/src/view/publisher.ts setBy fills, keeping only a fork's .lineage (theme.css:238-239). For an app, that line is now the header spec 2026-10-21-app-push-pull §5.5 asks for (\"by @owner\", \"vN by @editor\", the install count), and Get in Clax's links send phone visitors to exactly this page. At 390 px an app page shows its title, Comment and the more menu; nothing says whose app it is.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":236},"end":{"line":236},"content_hash":"86368cd129600218bbb055be52770ef81bf6271ee2daf5670ea7a5f460c844b6"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the line for an app at phone width as for a fork (a class such as .app-by that the phone rule keeps, ellipsised on one line), or show the byline in the more menu's header on a phone.","summary":"At phone width the app's byline and install count are hidden, so a phone visitor sees no owner, version or installs on an app's page","tags":["app-push","ui","phone","review","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/failure.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T19:18:59.099851Z","id":"59ece9eac0583c5bdce2851092222a21fac07f8d9d8f056841df313285d37ff6","body":{"detail":"failure.ts COMMENTS_OFF (\"comments are off for this page\"), web/shell/src/caps/errors.ts:9 COMMENTS_OFF and web/shell/src/view/artifact-controller.ts:165 COMMENTS_OFF_TITLE (both \"Comments are off for this page\") say the same thing; a wording change must find all three, and the two exports named COMMENTS_OFF differ in case.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":22},"end":{"line":23},"content_hash":"09cd828c9edf956185c8b2c4356da89fc52e9ffdcde57daca21f7cfe8900ff6e"},"suggested_fix":"Keep one constant (the capitalised sentence) and lower-case it where failureText needs it after its prefix.","summary":"The comments-off sentence is defined three times","tags":["app-push","copy","review","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/waiting.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T06:35:53.967665Z","id":"92aa0e381a2dd9e1d56be3255fbacdd148c95f2b92e35902470441a4951adce2","body":{"detail":"web/shell/src/waiting.ts waitingLabel case \"withheld\" reads 'waiting for <approver>'s approval' ('waiting for your approval' when mine, '· the agent no longer has access' with no_access), added in f477d1815. web/shell/src/thread-owner.test.ts:76 'reads withheld as waiting for the approver's approval' expects \"waiting for Sam's approval\", and :162-167 cover no approver, mine and no_access; //web:unit passes on akesling/app-pp-fix-web. Proposed for close by the owner (reason: fixed).","kind":"comment","references":"ecad42f2c2c91864e3508cc7d720dc3bb984777ece85fc34b395af113c311017","summary":"Already fixed: waitingLabel has a withheld case since f477d1815","tags":["session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/failure.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T06:35:53.968471Z","id":"9142fca764a61f88eb5dacdd9f8535af9d965a4b6e9a2714fe9976ccf946f4e0","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:07a4da654","summary":"One constant, failure.ts COMMENTS_OFF (\"Comments are off for this page\"); failureText lower-cases it after its prefix, and caps/comments.ts, ShellSidebar.svelte and TopbarIsland.svelte import it. Test 'says a comments_off refusal as the one comments-off sentence, after its prefix' (web/shell/src/failure.test.ts); bazel test //web:lint //web:typecheck //web:unit: 3 tests pass. Mutation: changing COMMENTS_OFF alone fails 8 tests in failure.test.ts, new-comment.test.ts, topbar.test.ts and caps/comments.test.ts, so all surfaces read the one constant.","supersedes":"59ece9eac0583c5bdce2851092222a21fac07f8d9d8f056841df313285d37ff6","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/theme.css","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T06:35:54.193152Z","id":"28f44a06ac16e745f53e1b2285d39f3c7558dc2bc772dc413d4477d03707260a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:c9129b465","summary":"setBy marks an app's line .app and the phone rule keeps .ttl .by.app on one line (ellipsised), its lineage inline. web/e2e/sharing.spec.ts 'comments switch refuses a guest comment' checks .topbar .by visible with 'v1 · by Ada' at 390x844; publisher.test.ts checks the class. bazel test //web:e2e_rest --test_arg=--reporter=list --test_arg=e2e/sharing.spec.ts: passed; screenshots at 390 px, light and dark, show the byline. Mutation: without the two .by.app rules the e2e fails at toBeVisible (sharing.spec.ts:215).","supersedes":"f91181cad8e92c71e0a83ef104fb45d9eb260b09491ace1b5055ec23f8fdfa84","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:b2fb951f-3ceb-4c65-a7b7-a705e815488a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream-hub.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:10.090163Z","id":"83511928b32c9135b4fdd9a33163dd720c92e574f3e88b326ab3c7c1f357bb4f","body":{"detail":"The hub learns that the server carries /api/stream over a WebSocket only from a 426 to the plain request, and remembers it for its own life: once per shared worker, but once per page load where the hub runs in the tab (no SharedWorker). The daemon is unaffected. A server that advertised the transport (in the /a/ bootstrap, or a header on a response the shell already makes) would save the round trip on the time-to-usable path.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":369},"end":{"line":373},"content_hash":"e461307789815f4359eb9af3636cda0d5096499a69ff787f40b9ab7f66444374"},"summary":"On a Worker each new stream hub pays one 426 round trip before it opens the WebSocket","supersedes":"0de6d056a59b5f7f7b32fc7cf91489ac31c28b777c80bf66c6323de42479a24c","tags":["session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream-hub.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:10.151486Z","id":"c1651288f7d59d7fc03f9b0a7efd1c858f1f4c8a2a6161c8cee948bbe23b6e13","body":{"detail":"drop() aborts the current connection. When that connection is a GET /api/stream whose response has not reached the page yet, Chrome keeps the socket to drain the response for reuse (about 5 s; the SSE body never ends) and only then closes it, so the daemon counts the stream as attached meanwhile (`open` and `levels` in GET /api/_test/stream/open), holding a second stream for the browser. The hub reopens at most once per caller change (the `reconnect` case compares the asked caller with the one the stream's `ready` named), so this happens when a reopen, a reconnect after a refused subscription, or a failure's retry lands while a connect is in flight. The daemon detaches a closed client within a millisecond; the delay is the browser's.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":578},"end":{"line":584},"content_hash":"50f43433859ae4b4960306f84d9917ae901ccd99c2692329e7e275099aa83ca7"},"suggested_fix":"Let an in-flight connect reach its `ready` before acting on a reconnect or a refused subscription (decide then, as an ask made while no stream is up already is), so the hub never aborts a stream request that has not answered.","summary":"A stream request aborted before it answers stays open on the daemon for up to 5 s","supersedes":"f7af5d6e1ba912cfadc116fa2e4533c0f7961d5edba9479cab37d1dd306ab6d8","tags":["risk","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/waiting.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T16:57:10.444978Z","id":"f6564b72606146db4892c61812bdc54f527e5c4b9af580a2011f44d4d61af7d7","body":{"detail":"The daemon now reports state withheld with an approver name (crates/clax-core/src/store/feedback.rs state_of) for a comment held from its agent until the agent's person approves its author; waitingLabel has no case for it, so the thread shows no waiting indicator. Spec §10 wants 'waiting for Sam's approval'. clax comments prints it (crates/clax-cli/src/commands/comments.rs delivery).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":36},"end":{"line":36},"content_hash":"94752ffd9323a0e85d941ed8b7de2099267ddbfee318f8338c4977428961c9be"},"summary":"The shell shows no delivery label for feedback_state withheld","supersedes":"ecad42f2c2c91864e3508cc7d720dc3bb984777ece85fc34b395af113c311017","tags":["people","ui","spec:10","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:47:45.054407Z","id":"c141037d94313c3af90e38b6c8b776be4143590750526eebebda748edca110c4","body":{"detail":"A tab hidden for HIDDEN_MS (30 s) releases its topics and fetches its state again when it shows; the shared connection has no per-tab resume point.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":376},"end":{"line":395},"content_hash":"11c6d5ee1beb1295890e20b19fe7e77227a5b2282068b40db1965fce57d3b24b"},"suggested_fix":"Per-topic rings in the worker would let a briefly hidden tab replay instead.","summary":"A hidden tab's catch-up is a refetch","supersedes":"d8cce851555f951af6ccf1ae3b9dfe38ebb76efe1340bada4e9bc10a16ca795e","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-23T21:47:45.121777Z","id":"8e82bf470c89ef146a702e271c001000d99d25ca07f47dedabd4ead5919dab1c","body":{"detail":"A tab counts its hub gone after DEAD_MS (35 s) without a ping, or at once where the browser fires close on the worker's port. A worker that lives but hangs is not restarted, since a new SharedWorker of the same name reaches the same instance. Leader tabs are not pinged at all: a hidden leader's timers are throttled and its followers would replace it needlessly; a leader hidden for 30 s leaves, so a frozen tab does not hold the connection for long.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":497},"end":{"line":500},"content_hash":"179f7bffd3ea769b233434bd4f135364ef246a4fcfac38935bbe0a93776dccb1"},"summary":"The shared worker is checked only by its pings; a hung worker is not restarted","supersedes":"932a69a375afa3ab35f876ff67c6201fde3ec7fd4e715604f4bc917459b6d3df","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:cc23b85c-a691-4093-ab7a-f909d7a53e66"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/api.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T23:17:45.840941Z","id":"1c56cb8459c273f44bc3425f068d0e5a19043f17fcb958c5f93d9d89e4505a31","body":{"detail":"getToken shows the cold-browser page (web/shell/src/cold-browser.ts) on 401 no_credential from GET /api/token. A session ended while a page is open (local_trust::OwnerSessions::end) leaves the page's other requests failing 401 no_credential until it reloads, when the daemon serves the page itself.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":154},"end":{"line":154},"content_hash":"c0dd245a150e6b34ce365535a95245808530f74802b724bcf9d36dcf793108e8"},"summary":"The shell shows how to open Clax from the terminal only when its token request is refused for no credential","tags":["shell","local-trust","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/owner.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T08:56:22.821181Z","id":"a9735830bbbd181b391760f2bd4a752af06d49915d9149abfcca8e516b264ab3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a5019f38","span":{"start":{"line":24},"end":{"line":26},"content_hash":"9c970c33d9b46f3a88558e76a513e06786ad91e220ff45bdb65f608847714d05"},"summary":"Taken: inboxBrowser now reads the person flag of the page's own GET /api/viewers/me (the gallery's lookup, the artifact view's seeded viewer), else the owner's token; the inbox routes stay the authority when the feeds start. Evidence: e2e/questions.spec.ts, reverted to expect no /api/inbox or /api/questions request from a LAN viewer, passes; in Chromium a plain LAN viewer on /, /inbox and /a/<id> made none, and Ivy's and Jo's browsers made no /api/inbox?limit=1 look.","supersedes":"a9690820535f9d2d5c60dff24ad9b6e66d928e36ee3ef014608a3fa47676d2cf","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream-hub.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T08:56:23.400303Z","id":"8f2593c43feccdae3b534e964b178a75ad14651d2d0c66f063909d0d27385a98","body":{"detail":"The hub learns that the server carries /api/stream over a WebSocket only from a 426 to the plain request, and remembers it for its own life: once per shared worker, but once per page load where the hub runs in the tab (no SharedWorker). The daemon is unaffected. A server that advertised the transport (in the /a/ bootstrap, or a header on a response the shell already makes) would save the round trip on the time-to-usable path.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":368},"end":{"line":372},"content_hash":"e461307789815f4359eb9af3636cda0d5096499a69ff787f40b9ab7f66444374"},"summary":"On a Worker each new stream hub pays one 426 round trip before it opens the WebSocket","supersedes":"83511928b32c9135b4fdd9a33163dd720c92e574f3e88b326ab3c7c1f357bb4f","tags":["session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream-hub.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T08:56:23.493867Z","id":"9ac8965c1d4d504261633de3613c0a7be4488f4794477f45ca487adf1807cc69","body":{"detail":"Failure: in app mode (Hub env.host), a topic whose POST /api/stream/<id> the core answers 503 on every try. Each reopen's ready sets this.failures = 0 (stream-hub.ts:463), then the subscription answers 503 and fail() backs off from the first step again, so the backoff never grows and the stream reopens at the first step's wait indefinitely. web/shell/src/stream-hub.test.ts:731 (\"opens the stream again after a backoff, not at once, when a subscription answers 503\") pins the first wait only, and spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md:771 (\"`ready` resets the backoff\") produces this loop. A related case: a subscription answered unknown_stream (stream-hub.ts:704-709) calls connect() at once with no backoff, so a core that keeps answering it is asked in a tight loop on the host.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":461},"end":{"line":462},"content_hash":"0b7fdb9c4179ada304e7bad84c915bd4fdc134f37f65067ba2c44bb3565a4d25"},"suggested_fix":"Reset failures only when a subscription succeeds (the POST answers 2xx), not at ready, and give the unknown_stream reconnect the same backoff; amend spec 5.2's wording to match. Add a unit case: a subscription answering 503 every time waits longer on each reopen.","summary":"On the app's host a subscription the core keeps answering 5xx reopens the stream about every 0.5 s forever: ready resets failures before the subscription is asked","supersedes":"591dd598171597ad24d8134b412f6706bdfc23a4f5c7fa9b67c646dcdbadc70a","tags":["status:needs-decision","review","app-mode","stream","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream-hub.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T08:56:23.586261Z","id":"a634a65c949f546da285b16ddc6ea76655ee5f36e72f8a11b8a982b5be321a6a","body":{"detail":"drop() aborts the current connection. When that connection is a GET /api/stream whose response has not reached the page yet, Chrome keeps the socket to drain the response for reuse (about 5 s; the SSE body never ends) and only then closes it, so the daemon counts the stream as attached meanwhile (`open` and `levels` in GET /api/_test/stream/open), holding a second stream for the browser. The hub reopens at most once per caller change (the `reconnect` case compares the asked caller with the one the stream's `ready` named), so this happens when a reopen, a reconnect after a refused subscription, or a failure's retry lands while a connect is in flight. The daemon detaches a closed client within a millisecond; the delay is the browser's.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":577},"end":{"line":583},"content_hash":"50f43433859ae4b4960306f84d9917ae901ccd99c2692329e7e275099aa83ca7"},"suggested_fix":"Let an in-flight connect reach its `ready` before acting on a reconnect or a refused subscription (decide then, as an ask made while no stream is up already is), so the hub never aborts a stream request that has not answered.","summary":"A stream request aborted before it answers stays open on the daemon for up to 5 s","supersedes":"01855306804696538c10278736c341e4ab9f59455ac7efccfbf0ef159b63d35f","tags":["risk","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/stream-hub.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T08:56:23.679144Z","id":"084e399ecca246715c3adc7a6b46b38e6c999190a49dc20d7ccce54ae8c4d28e","body":{"detail":"drop() aborts the current connection. When that connection is a GET /api/stream whose response has not reached the page yet, Chrome keeps the socket to drain the response for reuse (about 5 s; the SSE body never ends) and only then closes it, so the daemon counts the stream as attached meanwhile (`open` and `levels` in GET /api/_test/stream/open), holding a second stream for the browser. The hub reopens at most once per caller change (the `reconnect` case compares the asked caller with the one the stream's `ready` named), so this happens when a reopen, a reconnect after a refused subscription, or a failure's retry lands while a connect is in flight. The daemon detaches a closed client within a millisecond; the delay is the browser's.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":577},"end":{"line":583},"content_hash":"50f43433859ae4b4960306f84d9917ae901ccd99c2692329e7e275099aa83ca7"},"suggested_fix":"Let an in-flight connect reach its `ready` before acting on a reconnect or a refused subscription (decide then, as an ask made while no stream is up already is), so the hub never aborts a stream request that has not answered.","summary":"A stream request aborted before it answers stays open on the daemon for up to 5 s","supersedes":"c1651288f7d59d7fc03f9b0a7efd1c858f1f4c8a2a6161c8cee948bbe23b6e13","tags":["risk","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/owner.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-30T08:56:23.774361Z","id":"a7379c12585b7c1f62807db19dbc9c138c343c3174d8fab7a6793c6d2006ed0d","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"43f48499256305c81642d0decec018ccd2d5734c316d1e9ac38c6ab8d1fdc9a0","summary":"Drifted and not re-anchored: the lines this record hashed (web/shell/src/owner.ts:13:15 at 2bbefe713, origin/main) were changed by branch remote-instances; its longest line, `export async function ownerBrowser(signal?: AbortSignal): Promise<boolean> {`, is now at line 14, but the lines around it changed. Whether the record still applies, and where, is for its author or the owner to judge.","tags":["drift","session:claude-code:988152cb-8f78-4b12-acdd-a455490bed05"]}}
